    <string name="sampling_label_temperature">Temperature</string>
    <string name="sampling_hint_temperature">Temperature controls model creativity. Low settings create more conservative, predictable responses. Higher settings allow more variety, but settings that are too high can make replies less coherent.\n\nGeneral Recommended Default: 0.7</string>
    <string name="streaming_title">Streaming</string>
    <string name="streaming_description">Show replies as they’re generated. When off, display the full reply only after it finishes.\n\nGeneral Recommended Default: On</string>
    <string name="sampling_label_top_p">Top P</string>
    <string name="sampling_hint_top_p">Top P controls how wide a pool of likely next words the model may choose from. A low value makes it stick to safer, more predictable wording. A higher value allows more variety, but can also make writing more rambling or inconsistent.\n\nGeneral Recommended Default: 1</string>
    <string name="sampling_label_frequency_penalty">Frequency Penalty</string>
    <string name="sampling_hint_frequency_penalty">Frequency Penalty discourages the model from repeating words or phrases it has already used. Positive values reduce repetition. Negative values allow more repetition. Values that are too strong can make replies sound unnatural or avoid necessary terms.\n\nGeneral Recommended Default: 0</string>
    <string name="sampling_label_presence_penalty">Presence Penalty</string>
    <string name="sampling_hint_presence_penalty">Presence Penalty discourages the model from returning to topics or ideas it has already mentioned. Positive values encourage new topics. Negative values encourage it to stay with existing topics. Values that are too strong can make replies scattered or repetitive.\n\nGeneral Recommended Default: 0</string>
