    <string name="usage_estimate_info_title">Best Estimated Usage</string>
    <string name="usage_estimate_info_body">Usage calculations reflect the best available data returned by the provider. Figures are rounded estimates and may not exactly match final billing statements. Final charges from your provider may differ slightly due to rounding, tiered rates, or dynamic processing fees.\n\nThe token number shown on an individual AI or user message is separate from this screen. It is an app estimate of only the visible text in that one message. It does not include conversation history, instructions, memory, attachments, tools, reasoning, or other request data sent to the model.\n\nDefinitions\n\nInput Tokens: Everything sent to the model for a request. This can include conversation history, instructions, memory, attachments, and tool information. The provider reports this count when available. If it is unavailable, the app estimates it when possible.\n\nCached Tokens: Input tokens the provider reused from an earlier request instead of processing again. Cached tokens are already included in Input Tokens; they are not added on top. If the provider does not report the cached portion, it says Not Reported.\n\nNot Cached: Input tokens that were not reported as reused from the cache. This includes newly processed input and may include tokens written into a new cache.\n\nOutput Tokens: Tokens generated by the model for the request. Provider-reported Output may already include billed reasoning, so reasoning is not added twice.\n\nCache Hit Rate: The percentage of all input tokens that the provider reported as reused from cache.\n\nCost: The provider\'s reported charge when available. Otherwise, the app estimates cost from the reported or estimated token counts and the prices saved when the request was made.\n\nNot Reported: The provider did not supply enough information and the app cannot calculate the value reliably.</string>
